{
    "background_story": "Buttercup was a gentle mare with a mischievous streak. She loved to wander away from her pasture and explore the surrounding countryside. Her owners would often find her loitering by the old oak tree, munching on the sweet grass that grew in its shade. Buttercup's favorite pastime was watching the world go by, and she'd spend hours grazing by the roadside, observing the humans and animals that passed through. Despite her tendency to loiter, Buttercup was a hard worker and would always return to her duties as a therapy horse, bringing joy and comfort to those who visited her. Her owners would chuckle at her antics, knowing that Buttercup's loitering was just a sign of her curious and affectionate nature.",
